A URL bookmark must round trip, and a failure must say so.

Every bookmark primitive in this port returned NULL or false with a TODO beside it, and none of
them set the error. CFURLCreateBookmarkData, CFURLCreateByResolvingBookmarkData,
CFURLCreateBookmarkDataFromFile, CFURLWriteBookmarkDataToFile, the two resource property readers
and CFURLResourceIsReachable. A document application cannot remember a file without them.

RETURNING NIL WITHOUT SETTING THE ERROR IS A COMBINATION macOS NEVER PRODUCES, and it is the half
that made this fatal rather than merely missing. Measured end to end in iA Writer:

  +[IAFileBookmark bookmarkDataWithURL:error:] answers nil and leaves the error nil
  its addURL: block reads the nil data, skips the create, and because the error is ALSO nil takes
  the branch that adds the bookmark to the array, so it adds a NIL
  -[NSMutableArray addObject:] here calls CFArrayAppendValue with NULL rather than raising as
  macOS does, so the nil lands in the array
  -[IAFileBookmarkHistory willUpdate:] enumerates that array, [nil identifier] answers nil, and
  removeObjectForKey: raises Cannot remove a nil key

CIDER_ENUM printed the deciding line on the run that died:

  CIDER_ENUM count=1 opts=0x2 nils=1 firstNil=0 first=(nil)

opts 0x2 is NSEnumerationReverse, which is the enumeration in willUpdate:, and the one element is
nil. The element was never a bookmark with a missing identifier, which is what three earlier
theories assumed and what the probe had already refuted.

BOOKMARK DATA IS OPAQUE ON macOS, which is what makes this implementable at all: nothing outside
the framework parses one, so any format round trips as long as create and resolve agree. The blob
here records a magic, a version, the device and inode at creation, and the path. Staleness is then
answered rather than guessed: the file is stale when it exists at the path but is a different inode.

Every exit either returns a blob or fills the error, including the ones that refuse.

tests/foundation/probe_bookmark_identity.m covers it with controls on both sides: an absent path is
NOT reachable, junk fails AND sets an error, a replaced file resolves and reports stale, and a
deleted file fails and sets an error. 36 checks, 0 mismatched.

